Descriptor-reuse A/B on the pod's hybridles tree
================================================

Question: the pod's deepmd-les tree predated commit b74a0bf (descriptor reuse), so
HybridLESModel.forward built a second neighbour list and called the descriptor again
instead of reusing the one the short-range path had already produced. Did that stale
tree also compute anything DIFFERENT, or only more?

Method: /tmp/les_ab.py builds the arm's model from one inline config, monkeypatches
DescrptSeA.forward to count calls, and runs one forward of the same single frame.
With no argument it saves the state dict; with a path it loads that state dict first,
so the two trees are compared at identical weights on identical input.

    CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES= OMP_NUM_THREADS=4 /root/venv310/bin/python /tmp/les_ab.py
    CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES= OMP_NUM_THREADS=4 /root/venv310/bin/python /tmp/les_ab.py /tmp/les_ab_state.pt

The stale tree was measured by temporarily restoring the 15 pre-update source files,
then re-applying b74a0bf; the tree's final state was verified by md5 afterwards.

