------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The `les` package: pod revision vs local, on a trained checkpoint
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The patch above covered the deepmd files but not the `les` package, and the two
trees' `les` packages are not the same revision: `les/src/les/les.py` differs
(pod 2026-09-20 01:58) and local has `module/charge_eq.py` and
`tests/test_charge_eq.py`, which the pod does not.

Read as a diff, every difference is one of two kinds and neither is reachable here:

  * `ewald.py` - the pod's file is byte-identical to local in every region it has.
    Local only adds `compute_coulomb_matrix`, used solely by charge_eq. One diff
    hunk, delete-to-match, zero pod-only lines.
  * `les.py` - the differences are the `charge_eq` / `charge_eq_debug` /
    `q_nn_debug` / `e_lr_graph_debug` feature set and its logging plumbing, all
    default-off. The arm's `les_params` sets none of those keys (checked against
    the generated input.yaml: local_charge, n_hidden, n_layers, add_linear_nn,
    sigma, dl, remove_self_interaction, output_scaling_factor, lr_weight, verbose,
    log_freq - and every one of them is read identically by both revisions).
    `lr_weight` is not in `les.py` at all; it is read by the patched
    `hybridles_model.py:82`, which is the same file on both sides.

Inspection is not the standard the rest of this work is held to, so it was
measured: `les_rev_check.py` (beside this log) loads the arm's own
`s8/model.ckpt-45000.pt`, evaluates two validation frames on CPU, and prints E, two
force vectors, |F| and the virial at full float precision. Run with
`DP_INTERFACE_PREC=low` on both trees (these checkpoints were trained in fp32) and
the same interpreter settings:

    E            = -277.25263848900795, -277.9975953698158
    F[0,0]       = -0.06409169733524323, 1.078971028327942, -1.1022361516952515
    F[1,-1]      = 0.2632662355899811, 0.9581760168075562, 0.7262380719184875
    |F|          = 74.83953094482422
    V sum        = -378.2880769688636

Identical to the last digit on both trees (`les` module file in both runs:
`/root/app/deepmd-les/deepmd-les/les/src/les/__init__.py`, each side's own copy).
So the pod's older `les` and local's current one are the same function for this
arm's config, and scoring these checkpoints locally measures the model that was
trained rather than a model plus a kernel revision difference.
